STEP 1 — Update the Dashboard Controller
Open controllers/adminController.js (or wherever your dashboard() function is).

Immediately after your User Statistics section (or after you calculate premiumUsers), add this:

// ===============================
// User Growth Analytics
// ===============================

const userGrowth = await User.aggregate([

    {

        $group: {

            _id: {

                year: { $year: "$createdAt" },

                month: { $month: "$createdAt" }

            },

            total: {

                $sum: 1

            }

        }

    },

    {

        $sort: {

            "_id.year": 1,

            "_id.month": 1

        }

    }

]);
This tells MongoDB:

"Group every user according to the month they registered."

For example, if your database contains:

User A   January
User B   January
User C   February
User D   March
User E   March
MongoDB returns something like:

[
    {
        _id: { year: 2026, month: 1 },
        total: 2
    },
    {
        _id: { year: 2026, month: 2 },
        total: 1
    },
    {
        _id: { year: 2026, month: 3 },
        total: 2
    }
]
That's exactly what Chart.js wants.

