That's exactly what Chart.js expects.

Then pass them to the view
In your res.render() call, add:

growthLabels,
growthData,
So the render object will include them alongside the other dashboard variables.

Why this transformation?
Instead of making the browser understand MongoDB's aggregation format:

{
    _id: {
        year: 2026,
        month: 7
    },
    total: 12
}
we simplify it on the server to:

labels = ["Jan 26", "Feb 26", "Mar 26"]

data = [5, 8, 11]
This keeps dashboard.js focused purely on rendering charts rather than processing database results.

