Step 2 — Extend window.dashboardData
Find your existing object:

window.dashboardData = {

    won: ...,

    lost: ...,

    ...

    free: ...,

    premium: ...

};
Extend it like this:

window.dashboardData = {

    won: <%= wonPredictions %>,
    lost: <%= lostPredictions %>,
    pending: <%= pendingPredictions %>,
    void: <%= voidPredictions %>,
    expired: <%= expiredPredictions %>,

    free: <%= freePredictions %>,
    premium: <%= premiumPredictions %>,

    growthLabels: <%- JSON.stringify(growthLabels) %>,
    growthData: <%- JSON.stringify(growthData) %>

};
Why JSON.stringify()?
Unlike numbers, these are arrays.

Without it, you'll end up with invalid JavaScript. Using:

<%- JSON.stringify(growthLabels) %>
produces valid array literals like:

["Jul 26", "Aug 26", "Sep 26"]
