how do i place it as the last item inside the Promise.all() array:

Good question. This is one of those JavaScript patterns that's much easier to understand when you see the "before" and "after".

Your current Promise.all()
Right now, it ends like this:

Prediction.find()
    .sort({ kickoffTime: -1 })
    .limit(5)
    .populate("createdBy", "username"),

User.find()
    .select("username email role subscriptionStatus createdAt")
    .sort({ createdAt: -1 })
    .limit(5)

]);
Notice the last item in the array is:

User.find()
    .select("username email role subscriptionStatus createdAt")
    .sort({ createdAt: -1 })
    .limit(5)
This is exactly where the aggregation goes.
Change the end of the array to this:

Prediction.find()
    .sort({ kickoffTime: -1 })
    .limit(5)
    .populate("createdBy", "username"),

User.find()
    .select("username email role subscriptionStatus createdAt")
    .sort({ createdAt: -1 })
    .limit(5),

User.aggregate([

    {
        $group: {

            _id: {

                year: { $year: "$createdAt" },

                month: { $month: "$createdAt" }

            },

            total: {

                $sum: 1

            }

        }

    },

    {
        $sort: {

            "_id.year": 1,

            "_id.month": 1

        }

    }

])

]);
The important part is the comma after:

.limit(5),
That comma tells JavaScript:

"There's one more promise coming."

Then the aggregation becomes the final promise in the array.

Then change the destructuring
At the top you currently have:

const [
    totalPredictions,
    premiumPredictions,
    freePredictions,
    pendingPredictions,
    wonPredictions,
    lostPredictions,
    voidPredictions,
    expiredPredictions,
    totalUsers,
    premiumUsers,
    latestPredictions,
    recentUsers
] = await Promise.all([
Simply add userGrowth as the last variable:

const [
    totalPredictions,
    premiumPredictions,
    freePredictions,
    pendingPredictions,
    wonPredictions,
    lostPredictions,
    voidPredictions,
    expiredPredictions,
    totalUsers,
    premiumUsers,
    latestPredictions,
    recentUsers,
    userGrowth
] = await Promise.all([
Notice how the order matches exactly:

Promise	Variable
Prediction.countDocuments()	totalPredictions
Prediction.countDocuments({ isPremium: true })	premiumPredictions
...	...
User.find()	recentUsers
User.aggregate()	userGrowth
That's the key rule with Promise.all():

The variables on the left must be in the same order as the promises on the right.

Finally
Delete this block entirely because it's now redundant:

const userGrowth = await User.aggregate([
    ...
]);
The userGrowth variable will already contain the aggregation result from Promise.all().

