100 users

10,000 users

server-side search scales much better than downloading every user to the browser.

Step 1 — Add a search box
Inside views/admin/users.ejs, above the table, add:

<form method="GET" action="/admin/users" class="mb-4">

    <div class="input-group">

        <input
            type="text"
            name="search"
            class="form-control"
            placeholder="Search username or email..."
            value="<%= search || '' %>"
        >

        <button class="btn btn-primary">

            <i class="bi bi-search"></i>

            Search

        </button>

    </div>

</form>
Step 2 — Update the controller
Replace this:

const users = await User.find()

    .sort({ createdAt: -1 });
with:

const search = req.query.search || "";

const query = {};

if (search) {

    query.$or = [

        {

            username: {

                $regex: search,

                $options: "i"

            }

        },

        {

            email: {

                $regex: search,

                $options: "i"

            }

        }

    ];

}

const users = await User.find(query)

    .sort({ createdAt: -1 });
Step 3 — Pass search back to the view
Update your res.render():

res.render("admin/users", {

    pageTitle: "Manage Users",

    users,

    search

});
Now the search box remembers what you typed after the page reloads.

Expected behavior
If your database contains:

Username	Email
rudolphbull	rudolph@gmail.com
john	john@yahoo.com
mary	mary@gmail.com
Searching for:

gmail
returns:

rudolphbull
mary
Searching for:

rud
returns:

rudolphbull
Searching for:

xyz
returns an empty table.

