There's one more place I'd like us to improve: your global error handler. Right now, it's probably rendering the 500 page with only a pageTitle or just the error object. We can update it to always provide pageTitle, message, details, and error in a consistent way, so every unexpected exception gets the same polished treatment without repeating logic in individual controllers.

If you paste your global error-handling middleware from app.js (or wherever you've defined it), we can make the entire error-handling flow consistent with the templates we've just refactored.


//Global Error Handler
app.use((err, req, res, next) => {
    console.log("Global error handler");
    console.error(err);

    res.status(500).render("500", {
        pageTitle: "Error",
        message: err.message
    });
